I'm adding some space before some rather severe SPOILERS....


















































1. In the early game, STOP KILLING MONSTERS! Nethack in the early game
gets exponentially more difficult when you crank up your experience and
levels. Leave that task to your familiar. You want to high level big
healthy cat with you as you wander around. So let the cat kill. Let the
cat eat. You pray for sustenance when you are weak. The only exception
in the early game are newts, because they may give you a point or two
of extra power when eaten. The kills only cost 1 point each.

2. Gather money. Sell everything you can afford at the shop. If you
personally are of other than lawful alignment for game playing then
invest in credit cloning (look in google groups for the term)

3. Don't be afraid to wear armor in the early game. You're being passive
which means that you won't have to cast a whole lot of spells.

4. 1-3 serve the single purpose of the early game: Get to the Minetown
priest(ess) and buy all the protection you can afford. Xanthian and I
often disagree to what degree to purchase. First out I usually just
keep paying until the priest(ess) doesn't automatically give the 
protection, generally a naked AC of 1. With some patience you can get
a lot lower. One issue to be careful of: a maxed out cat loves to
snack on the Minetown guards. Unfortunately the watch captain is usually
strong enough to take the cat out.

5. Now you're in midgame. A low AC and a strong pet will carry you
a long long way. Now it's time to start spellcasting. Ditch as much
of the metal armor as you can at this point. Try to get sleep, healing,
and identify going.

Try this method. You'll find you'll go a lot further than ramping up
your levels without it.

